# Consumer-side .npmrc — put this in the ROOT of any project that wants to install
# @disrptiv-exchange/apm-tool from GitHub Packages.
#
# 1. Copy this file to your project as `.npmrc`.
# 2. Create a GitHub personal access token (classic) at
#    https://github.com/settings/tokens with the `read:packages` scope.
# 3. Export it as GITHUB_TOKEN before running npm install:
#       export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx
#       npm install @disrptiv-exchange/apm-tool
#    Or for CI: set GITHUB_TOKEN as a repo secret and reference it the same way.
#
# Keep your real .npmrc out of git — gitignore it if it contains a hard-coded token.

@disrptiv-exchange:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
